From: RV220W OpenWrt promotion toolkit
Subject: [PATCH] MIPS: Octeon: clean up fixed-DT export and BootBus flash ownership

The Octeon setup code mutates the flat device tree while filling MAC
addresses, after the common OF code has recorded its CRC. Re-run the normal
verification helper with the DT virtual and physical addresses after Octeon's
fixups so /sys/firmware/fdt exports the actual tree rather than rejecting it as changed.

The historical Octeon flash driver and generic physmap both match cfi-flash.
Allow a board DTS to select the BootBus-aware driver explicitly. That driver
reads the live chip-select register programmed by U-Boot and therefore retains
the proven 32 MiB mapping without an intentionally failing generic probe.

Linux 6.12 requires both the virtual and physical DT addresses for
early_init_dt_verify(); the physical address is recovered with __pa() from the
linear-mapped Octeon DT pointer.

The setup.c hunk intentionally uses only the stable fill-MAC/unflatten tail as
context. OpenWrt's earlier 400-ubnt_dts_pruning.patch modifies the surrounding
board-selection and pruning code, so including that block in the hunk makes the
patch version-fragile.

--- a/arch/mips/cavium-octeon/setup.c
+++ b/arch/mips/cavium-octeon/setup.c
@@ -1228,5 +1228,11 @@ void __init device_tree_init(void)
 	if (fill_mac)
 		octeon_fill_mac_addresses();
+
+	/* Octeon fixups mutate the flat tree after OF recorded its CRC. */
+	if (!early_init_dt_verify(initial_boot_params,
+				  __pa(initial_boot_params)))
+		panic("Corrupt Device Tree after Octeon fixups.");
+
 	unflatten_and_copy_device_tree();
 	init_octeon_system_type();
 }
--- a/arch/mips/cavium-octeon/flash_setup.c
+++ b/arch/mips/cavium-octeon/flash_setup.c
@@ -122,5 +122,8 @@ static int octeon_flash_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 
 static const struct of_device_id of_flash_match[] = {
+	{
+		.compatible = "cavium,octeon-3860-bootbus-flash",
+	},
 	{
 		.compatible = "cfi-flash",
 	},
-- 
